FILE 7: codemind/agentguard/pr_enforcer.py

Class: PREnforcer

Entry point. Called by GitHub webhook handler.
Orchestrates the full pipeline.

Dependencies: all above classes, TachyonClient,
AgentGraph, GitHub API (httpx)

Constructor:
  agent_graph: AgentGraph
  scanner: AgentScanner
  detector: BreakingChangeDetector
  recommender: FixRecommender
  reporter: PRReporter
  tachyon: TachyonClient
  db: AsyncIOMotorDatabase
  github_token: str  # from GITHUB_TOKEN env var

async enforce(pr_payload: dict) -> PRReport
  pr_payload is the raw GitHub PR webhook body.

  Step 1 — Extract changed files
    GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{number}/files
    via GitHub API
    Filter to files that match agent patterns:
      *.py containing StateGraph or @agent
      agent.yaml, agent.json, agent.yml
      *.py containing @router.post with LLM body

  Step 2 — Fetch file contents
    For each changed file:
      GET raw content from PR head branch
      GET raw content from PR base branch
      (base = pre-PR version for comparison)

  Step 3 — Scan both versions
    For each changed file:
      new_defs = scanner.scan_file(
        file_path, new_content, repo_id)
      old_defs = scanner.scan_file(
        file_path, old_content, repo_id)
    Match by agent_id within same file

  Step 4 — Detect changes
    For each (old_def, new_def) pair:
      changes = detector.detect(old_def, new_def)

  Step 5 — Find affected downstream agents
    For each changed agent with CRITICAL changes:
      downstream = agent_graph.get_downstream_agents(
        agent_id)
    For each downstream agent:
      relevant_changes = filter changes that
        affect interfaces this agent depends on
        (match via edge.interface_ref)

  Step 6 — Get fix recommendations
    For each affected agent + relevant change:
      fix = await recommender.recommend(
        change, changed_agent,
        affected_agent, tachyon)
    Build AffectedAgent with fix populated

  Step 7 — Build report
    report = reporter.build_report(...)

  Step 8 — Post GitHub PR comment
    POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}
         /comments
    Body: report.report_markdown
    Retry: exponential backoff, max 3 attempts
    On final failure: log error, do not raise
      (report is already built, comment failure
       should not break the pipeline)

  Step 9 — Set GitHub Check status
    POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/statuses/{sha}
    state: "failure" | "neutral" | "success"
    context: "AgentGuard"
    description: summary line (max 140 chars)

  Return report

_filter_agent_files(
  files: list[dict]
) -> list[dict]
  - files is GitHub API file objects
    [{filename, status, additions, deletions}]
  - Return files where filename matches:
    *.py AND (StateGraph OR @agent OR
    @register_agent OR tachyon OR langchain)
    OR filename in [agent.yaml, agent.json,
    agent.yml]
    OR filename matches **/agent.yaml pattern
  - status filter: only "modified" or "added"
    (deleted files handled separately)

async _handle_deleted_files(
  deleted_files: list[str],
  repo_id: str
) -> None
  - For each deleted file: scan old content
    for agent definitions
  - For each found agent_id:
    downstream = agent_graph.get_downstream_agents
    If downstream not empty:
      Add to report as TOOL_REMOVED CRITICAL
    await agent_graph.remove_agent(agent_id, db)

